      {
        "key": null,
        "edge": "contain",
        "value": {
          "kind": "scalar",
          "value": "A link's target is a **sigiled pointer**. This guide tours every tier: document-relative\nlinks at [*:1](*:1), project-rooted ones at [*:2](*:2), the parent and current scopes\nat [*:3](*:3), the read-forever aliases and legacy spellings at [*:4](*:4), and external\ntargets at [*:5](*:5) — each its own subchapter below.\n",
          "array": false,
          "set": false,
          "yo": false,
          "anchors": [],
          "entries": []
        }
      },
      {
        "key": null,
        "edge": "contain",
        "value": {
          "kind": "scalar",
          "value": "Document-relative links",
          "array": true,
          "set": false,
          "yo": false,
          "anchors": [],
          "entries": [
            {
              "key": null,
              "edge": "contain",
              "value": {
                "kind": "scalar",
                "value": "A `*:path` link counts from **this document** — the whole guide — however deep you are\nreading, and a bare integer segment is a position. The title is the self-value and\nconsumes no index, so the intro is [*:0](*:0) and this section is [*:1](*:1).\n",
                "array": false,
                "set": false,
                "yo": false,
                "anchors": [],
                "entries": []
              }
            },
            {
              "key": null,
              "edge": "contain",
              "value": {
                "kind": "scalar",
                "value": "Going deeper",
                "array": true,
                "set": false,
                "yo": false,
                "anchors": [],
                "entries": [
                  {
                    "key": null,
                    "edge": "contain",
                    "value": {
                      "kind": "scalar",
                      "value": "Two levels down, a `*:…` link still counts from the document root: the intro at\n[*:0](*:0), the external-targets section at [*:5](*:5), or this very line\nat [*:1:1:0](*:1:1:0).\n",
                      "array": false,
                      "set": false,
                      "yo": false,
                      "anchors": [],
                      "entries": []
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "key": null,
        "edge": "contain",
        "value": {
          "kind": "scalar",
          "value": "Project-root links",
          "array": true,
          "set": false,
          "yo": false,
          "anchors": [],
          "entries": [
            {
              "key": null,
              "edge": "contain",
              "value": {
                "kind": "scalar",
                "value": "A `*::path` link is anchored at the **project root** — the directory yamlover was\nserved. Served from the repo, a sibling example is at\n[*::examples:68-math-chapter](*::examples:68-math-chapter), or one formula in it\nat [*::examples:68-math-chapter:2](*::examples:68-math-chapter:2).\n",
                "array": false,
                "set": false,
                "yo": false,
                "anchors": [],
                "entries": []
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "key": null,
        "edge": "contain",
        "value": {
          "kind": "scalar",
          "value": "Parent and current scope",
          "array": false,
          "set": false,
          "yo": false,
          "anchors": [],
          "entries": [
            {
              "key": "notes",
              "edge": "contain",
              "value": {
                "kind": "scalar",
                "value": "a keyed member of this section — `*notes` lands here",
                "array": false,
                "set": false,
                "yo": false,
                "anchors": [],
                "entries": []
              }
            },
            {
              "key": null,
              "edge": "contain",
              "value": {
                "kind": "scalar",
                "value": "A `*name` link resolves in the mapping the prose belongs to — this section's own note\nis at [*notes](*notes). A `*..:` link starts one level up: from here the parent is the\nguide itself, so its intro is at [*..:0](*..:0) and the previous section\nat [*..:2](*..:2).\n",
                "array": false,
                "set": false,
                "yo": false,
                "anchors": [],
                "entries": []
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "key": null,
        "edge": "contain",
        "value": {
          "kind": "scalar",
          "value": "Aliases and legacy spellings",
          "array": true,
          "set": false,
          "yo": false,
          "anchors": [],
          "entries": [
            {
              "key": null,
              "edge": "contain",
              "value": {
                "kind": "scalar",
                "value": "The **bare colon** form is the same pointer without its sigil, and reads **forever** as\nan alias — the intro at [:0](:0) still lands, though the sigiled spelling is what the\nengine writes when a move rewrites a link.\n",
                "array": false,
                "set": false,
                "yo": false,
                "anchors": [],
                "entries": []
              }
            },
            {
              "key": null,
              "edge": "contain",
              "value": {
                "kind": "scalar",
                "value": "The **slash** spellings are legacy-frozen: the document-relative [/0](/0) and the\nproject-rooted [//examples/68-math-chapter](//examples/68-math-chapter) still navigate,\nwritten never.\n",
                "array": false,
                "set": false,
                "yo": false,
                "anchors": [],
                "entries": []
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "key": null,
        "edge": "contain",
        "value": {
          "kind": "scalar",
          "value": "External targets and the reserved sigil",
          "array": true,
          "set": false,
          "yo": false,
          "anchors": [],
          "entries": [
            {
              "key": null,
              "edge": "contain",
              "value": {
                "kind": "scalar",
                "value": "Any target with a scheme is an **external** link, opened in a new tab: the KaTeX\nproject at [https://katex.org](https://katex.org), or mail the maintainer\nat [mailto:dimskraft@gmail.com](mailto:dimskraft@gmail.com).\n",
                "array": false,
                "set": false,
                "yo": false,
                "anchors": [],
                "entries": []
              }
            },
            {
              "key": null,
              "edge": "contain",
              "value": {
                "kind": "scalar",
                "value": "A `&…` target is **reserved** for bookmarks — it parses but does not yet navigate, so\nits label renders as plain text: [a future bookmark](&some-mark).\n",
                "array": false,
                "set": false,
                "yo": false,
                "anchors": [],
                "entries": []
              }
            }
          ]
        }
